PC-F02 independent review, one finding.

CONFIRMED and FIXED (medium, core/MediaSetup.lua:99): the file-load RegisterLSM
was the only registration, so an LSM embedded by an addon loading after
PrettyChat never received the Ka0s catalog. NS.RegisterMedia is published and
PrettyChat:OnEnable repeats it; RegisterLSM skips held keys. LibSharedMedia-3.0
added to the TOC OptionalDeps. Three new tests; the OnEnable test was seen red
without the call. Smoke SKIN-24 gains the load-after case (open, not passed).

Not fixed: the suggested alternative, vendoring LSM. The run forbids touching
libs/ other than by the re-vendor, so it is left to the owner. Consequently
PrettyChat alone (no LSM anywhere) still lists the leading row alone and draws
no Ka0s skin face, and an LSM first arriving via a load-on-demand addon after
login is not caught.
